\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {The road to Liese Academy hasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t changed, not in all these years.}
\par\plain {First, the Deep Woods. A name that sounds far more mysterious than it really is. In truth, it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s just miles of trees packed too close together, a canopy so thick the morning light can barely slip through. Riding under it always feels like diving into a tunnel of shadows\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 cold air in my lungs, damp earth under my tires, branches whispering secrets I\u8217\'92d rather not hear. The silence there presses close, broken only by the crunch of gravel beneath my wheels.}
\par\plain {I almost pedaled straight into them before I saw them: a knot of men gathered off the trail, half-hidden by the trees. Hunters, by the look of them. A patchwork of chain, leather, and dented steel. Half of them carried matchlock rifles so rusted I doubted they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d survive a spark, while the rest swung axes and swords like they\u8217\'92d been born with them.}
\par\plain {I skidded my bike to a stop, gravel crunching too loud in the hush. Every head turned.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Uh,\u8221\'94 I said, \u8220\'93what\u8217\'92s going on?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {A man with a goatee and a pike stepped forward. His armor was mostly leather, patched with someone else\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s chainmail. }
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Report of monster infestation in these parts,\u8221\'94 he said, voice gruff but not unfriendly. \u8220\'93What about you, boy? Where d\u8217\'92you live?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I live by the cliff,\u8221\'94 I said before I could think better of it. \u8220\'93At the old lighthouse.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {One of the Hunters\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 a woman with a scarred cheek\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 let out a sharp breath. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Past the woods? And no guards?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {I lifted a hand, trying to sound casual. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re fine. My mother... She kept us safe. Nothing gets to the Lighthouse so far.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {The leader\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eyes narrowed, then he gave a small, knowing nod. \u8220\'93Ah. So you\u8217\'92re one of them.\u8221\'94 His tone carried the weight of something I didn\u8217\'92t want unpacked here. \u8220\'93Carry on, then. But best be careful.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {The Hunters drifted back into their huddle, already talking of tracks and traps and things I didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t want to picture. I pushed off again, wheels cracking twigs as I left them behind\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 feeling the shadows a little heavier than before.}
\par\plain {Past the trees, the world opens up into Gunther\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s Farm. Wide fields stretching on both sides, dotted with lazy cows and the occasional scarecrow that looks one stiff breeze away from retirement. Old man Gunther waves if he sees you\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 he waved at me this morning, straw hat bobbing, the same way he has since I was twelve. Some things really don\u8217\'92t change.}
\par\plain {Then comes Weshaven. A town so modest it could probably fit inside a single King\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s Grave neighborhood. Cobblestone streets, shopkeepers sweeping their stoops, children chasing each other between market stalls. It smells like bread and smoke and horses, and for all its smallness, it has a heartbeat you can feel as you pass through.}
\par\plain {But the real trial waits at the end: the climb to Liese Academy. Nestled at the foot of the Easmund Hills, not quite high enough to be breathtaking, but steep enough to make your legs curse your existence. Back in the day, I used to do this ride so often my calves were carved out of stone. These days? Not so much. Halfway up, I was already wondering if I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d survive the climb or if they\u8217\'92d have to send Torrie home in mourning clothes.}
\par\plain {Still, as the spires of the Academy came into view\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 sharp and tall against the hills\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 I felt that familiar twist in my stomach. Memories waiting in those halls, and not all of them good.}}